WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.873 --> 00:00:19.686
Everything an instructor does starts from the kiosk.

2
00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:26.976
Tap Instructor, in the row under the two big buttons.

3
00:00:26.976 --> 00:00:30.164
The panel is behind your instructor PIN.

4
00:00:30.164 --> 00:00:34.395
Face ID is the shortcut — the PIN is what actually opens it.

5
00:00:34.395 --> 00:00:40.442
Type your six digits.

6
00:00:40.442 --> 00:00:45.805
Then tap Unlock.

7
00:00:45.805 --> 00:00:51.385
This is the Instructor Panel. Five tabs across the top.

8
00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:57.149
Open the Export tab.

9
00:00:57.149 --> 00:01:01.845
Attendance is exported a year at a time.

10
00:01:01.845 --> 00:01:07.695
Each year shows how many visits it holds.

11
00:01:07.695 --> 00:01:14.048
Pick the year, then tap Export.

12
00:01:14.048 --> 00:01:20.304
Now the iPad takes over. This is the standard share sheet.

13
00:01:20.304 --> 00:01:28.139
Choose Save to Files — this is the step people miss.

14
00:01:28.139 --> 00:01:34.447
It saves into On My iPad, in a Matdo Check folder.

15
00:01:34.447 --> 00:01:41.238
There it is. Tap it to open.

16
00:01:41.238 --> 00:01:48.220
One row per attendee, two columns per day — In and Out.

17
00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:57.367
The same layout the Windows app produced, so your old spreadsheets still line up.
